# data file for fldtk fluid (Fast Light User Interface Designer)
version 1.0000
comment {A live preview of the D source (and, separately, the `.fl`
project text) this project's own tree would currently generate, kept in
sync with whatever node is currently selected in the widget editor or
the project tree: selecting a node pans both text views to its own
generated block and highlights it, matching FLTK's own Code
View panel.

Ported from FLTK's fluid/panels/codeview_panel.fl, with a few
deliberate, disclosed scope adjustments rather than a full mechanical
translation:

 - No Header/Strings tabs. This dialect has no header/`.cxx` split (a
   single generated `.d` file per project, matching every other
   converted panel/sample so far) and no separate i18n *string-table
   export* (a `.po`/`.msg` catalog file) -- both entire tabs FLTK
   has simply don't apply here. Only Source (the generated D, via
   `fluid.code_writer.Writer`) and Project (the `.fl` text, via the
   already-real `fluid.project_writer.ProjectWriter`) remain. The
   project's own i18n *settings* (`fluid.i18n.I18nSettings`) ARE
   threaded through both remaining tabs though (`codeviewRefresh()`'s
   `i18n` parameter, `cvI18n_`) -- so a project with GNU/POSIX
   translation configured shows its real, wrapped `gettext(...)`/
   `catgets(...)` label/tooltip calls in the Source tab, not the plain
   unwrapped string literals a stale `i18n`-less call would show.
 - Node<->text-position sync covers `fluid.code_writer.Writer`'s
   widget-tree node kinds (window/group/widget, including a menu-owning
   widget's own array-literal block) in the Source tab, and every node
   kind in the Project tab (`fluid.project_writer.ProjectWriter.
   writeNode()` walks the whole tree uniformly). A node kind the Source
   tab doesn't track (Function, Class, decl, comment, ...) simply gets
   no Source-tab highlight when selected -- the same graceful no-op
   FLTK itself falls back to for any node with an untracked
   position (`fluid.node.Node.setupSpan`/`finalizeSpan` default to
   `TextSpan.init`, `start == -1`).
 - The "code choice" dropdown has three entries (instantiate/setup/
   finalize) rather than FLTK's five (prolog/static/instantiate/
   setup/finalize): this dialect has no header (folding "prolog", which
   FLTK itself just aliases to "instantiate", out) and no separate
   per-node "static data" phase distinct from "setup" (a `.fl` node's
   own declaration-shaped content -- e.g. a menu-owning widget's item
   array -- is written inline as part of its own block here, not to a
   separate pre-instantiation pass the way FLTK's menu/class
   declarations are).
 - The `Auto-Refresh` light button (`cvAutorefresh`) is real, gating
   `codeviewAutoRefresh()` -- the single function `gui_main.d` calls
   from every one of its own project-mutating entry points, in place of
   FLTK's own single `codeview_defer_update()` call site inside
   `Project::set_modflag()` (`fluid/Project.cxx`; this dialect has no
   equivalent centralized "mark modified" function, so `gui_main.d`
   calls `codeviewAutoRefresh()` directly at each of its own mutation
   sites instead, so the light button's value genuinely gates the
   refresh (a version that instead called
   `codeviewRefresh()` directly, unconditionally, whenever the panel was
   visible would make this light button decorative-only). One
   deliberate simplification from FLTK's own mechanism: no debounce
   timer (`Fl::add_timeout(0.5, ...)`) -- every call site already fires
   at most once per discrete edit (not per drag-frame), so there's
   nothing to coalesce; unchecking the button is a plain on/off gate on
   `codeviewAutoRefresh()`, not a rate limiter. The plain "Refresh"
   button stays unconditional either way. Every automatic refresh
   re-applies the current selection's highlight too
   (`codeviewUpdatePosition()`, called at the end of `codeviewRefresh()`),
   so toggling Auto-Refresh back on never loses the pan/highlight state.
 - `Fl_Text_Editor`-based `cv_source`/`cv_header` (FLTK) become
   plain `TextDisplay`s here (matching FLTK's own choice for its
   *other* two tabs, Strings/Project) -- nothing in this reduced scope
   needs `Fl_Text_Editor`'s extra editing affordances over
   `Fl_Text_Display`, since neither generated view is meant to be
   edited in place. `cvSource`/`cvProject` use
   `fluid.code_viewer.CodeViewer` (FLTK's `Code_Viewer`), which
   swaps the global selection color for a light gray around each
   `draw()` so the node highlight stays readable against the syntax
   colors.
 - Current-project state (`cvRoots_`) is a private module-level `Node[]`
   updated by whichever of `codeviewRefresh()`/`codeviewToggleVisibility()`
   the caller (`gui_main.d`) invokes with a fresh copy -- matching
   FLTK's own reliance on a single global (`Fluid.proj`) for the
   same purpose, just passed explicitly rather than read from a
   project-wide singleton this port doesn't have. `cvCurrent_` mirrors
   FLTK's own `Fluid.proj.tree.current` the same way, tracking
   whichever node the pan/highlight logic last ran for so the Tabs
   switch callback and the code-choice dropdown's own callback can
   re-apply it without needing the caller to pass it again. The
   "Reveal" button's reverse lookup (`findInText()`, text position ->
   Node) reports back to `gui_main.d` via `cvOnReveal`, a module-level
   delegate the caller assigns once during startup -- the same
   cross-module callback shape `fluid.function_panel`'s own
   `binButtonCb`/`codeButtonCb` already use, since `gui_main.d` already
   imports this module and a reverse import would cycle.
}
  {
    in_source
    in_header
  }
decl {import fluid;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
decl {Node[] cvRoots_;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
decl {I18nSettings cvI18n_;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
decl {bool cvDubHeader_;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
decl {ProjectSettings cvSettings_;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
decl {Node cvCurrent_;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
decl {/// Set once by gui_main.d during startup; called by the "Reveal"
/// button with the node found at the clicked text position and
/// whether the click was a double-click (matching FLTK's own
/// select_only(node); reveal_in_browser(node); if
/// (Fl::event_clicks()==1) node->open(); sequence in cb_Reveal()).
void delegate(Node, bool) cvOnReveal;}
  {
    public
    global
  }
Function makeCodeviewPanel()
  {
  }
  {
    Window codeviewPanel
      {
        label {Code View}
        callback {codeviewPanel.hide();}
        xywh {518 271 520 515}
        type Double
        resizable
      }
      {
        Tabs cvTab
          {
            callback {codeviewUpdatePosition(cvCurrent_);}
            xywh {10 10 500 440}
            selection_color 4
            labelcolor 7
            resizable
          }
          {
            Group {}
              {
                label {Source}
                xywh {10 35 500 415}
                labelsize 13
                resizable
              }
              {
                TextDisplay cvSource
                  {
                    xywh {10 40 500 410}
                    textsize 11
                    textfont 4
                    class CodeViewer
                    setup {o.buffer(new TextBuffer());
enableHighlighting(o);
o.linenumberWidth(60);
o.linenumberSize(11);}
                    resizable
                  }
              }
            Group {}
              {
                label {Project}
                xywh {10 35 500 415}
                labelsize 13
                hide
              }
              {
                TextDisplay cvProject
                  {
                    xywh {10 40 500 410}
                    textsize 11
                    textfont 4
                    class CodeViewer
                    setup {o.buffer(new TextBuffer());
o.linenumberWidth(60);
o.linenumberSize(11);}
                    resizable
                  }
              }
          }
        Group {}
          {
            xywh {10 460 500 20}
          }
          {
            Button cvFindTextCase
              {
                label {aA}
                xywh {244 460 25 20}
                labelsize 11
                type Toggle
              }
            Input cvFindText
              {
                label {Find:}
                callback {import std.string : toStringz;
TextDisplay e = cvSource.visibleR() ? cvSource : cvProject;
auto b = e.buffer();
int pos = e.insertPosition();
int found;
bool ok = b.searchForward(pos, cvFindText.value(), found, cvFindTextCase.value() != 0);
if (ok)
\{
    b.select(found, found + cast(int) cvFindText.value().length);
    e.insertPosition(found);
    e.showInsertPosition();
\}}
                xywh {40 460 200 20}
                labelsize 11
                textsize 11
                when 15
              }
            Button {}
              {
                label {<<}
                callback {TextDisplay e = cvSource.visibleR() ? cvSource : cvProject;
auto b = e.buffer();
string needle = cvFindText.value();
int pos = e.insertPosition() - 1;
if (pos < 0) pos = b.length() - 1;
int found;
bool ok = b.searchBackward(pos, needle, found, cvFindTextCase.value() != 0);
if (!ok) ok = b.searchBackward(b.length() - 1, needle, found, cvFindTextCase.value() != 0);
if (ok)
\{
    b.select(found, found + cast(int) needle.length);
    e.insertPosition(found);
    e.showInsertPosition();
\}}
                xywh {273 460 25 20}
                labelsize 11
              }
            Button {}
              {
                label {>>}
                callback {TextDisplay e = cvSource.visibleR() ? cvSource : cvProject;
auto b = e.buffer();
string needle = cvFindText.value();
int pos = e.insertPosition() + 1;
if (pos + 1 >= b.length()) pos = 0;
int found;
bool ok = b.searchForward(pos, needle, found, cvFindTextCase.value() != 0);
if (!ok && pos > 0) ok = b.searchForward(0, needle, found, cvFindTextCase.value() != 0);
if (ok)
\{
    b.select(found, found + cast(int) needle.length);
    e.insertPosition(found);
    e.showInsertPosition();
\}}
                xywh {298 460 25 20}
                labelsize 11
              }
            Button cvReveal
              {
                label {Reveal}
                callback {Node node;
if (cvSource.visibleR())
    node = findInText(0, cvSource.insertPosition());
else if (cvProject.visibleR())
    node = findInText(1, cvProject.insertPosition());
if (node !is null && cvOnReveal !is null)
    cvOnReveal(node, fl.core.eventClicks() == 1);}
                xywh {327 460 61 20}
                labelsize 11
              }
            Box {}
              {
                xywh {398 460 112 20}
                resizable
              }
          }
        Group {}
          {
            xywh {10 485 500 20}
          }
          {
            Button {}
              {
                label {Refresh}
                callback {codeviewRefresh(cvRoots_, cvI18n_, cvDubHeader_, cvSettings_);}
                xywh {10 485 61 20}
                labelsize 11
              }
            LightButton cvAutorefresh
              {
                label {Auto-Refresh}
                callback {codeviewRefresh(cvRoots_, cvI18n_, cvDubHeader_, cvSettings_);}
                xywh {78 485 91 20}
                labelsize 11
                value {1}
              }
            LightButton cvAutoposition
              {
                label {Auto-Position}
                xywh {176 485 90 20}
                labelsize 11
                value {1}
              }
            Choice cvCodeChoice
              {
                callback {codeviewUpdatePosition(cvCurrent_);}
                xywh {274 485 90 20}
                down_box BORDER_BOX
                labelsize 11
                textsize 11
              }
              {
                MenuItem {}
                  {
                    label {instantiate}
                  }
                MenuItem {}
                  {
                    label {setup}
                  }
                MenuItem {}
                  {
                    label {finalize}
                  }
              }
            Box {}
              {
                xywh {374 485 76 20}
                resizable
              }
            Button {}
              {
                label {Close}
                callback {codeviewPanel.hide();}
                xywh {460 485 50 20}
                labelsize 11
              }
          }
      }
  }
Function {codeviewRefresh(Node[] roots, I18nSettings i18n = I18nSettings.init, bool dubHeader = false, ProjectSettings settings = ProjectSettings.init)}
  {
    return_type void
  }
  {
    code {cvRoots_ = roots;
cvI18n_ = i18n;
cvDubHeader_ = dubHeader;
cvSettings_ = settings;
// `Writer.generate()` throws on a `.fl` property this dialect's own
// codegen doesn't recognize (an unknown boxtype/type/labeltype keyword
// -- see code_writer.d's translateBoxtype()/translateTypeWord()/
// translateLabeltype()) -- a real, expected case here specifically,
// since this panel can be refreshed against a hand-edited or foreign
// `.fl` file mid-session, not just a project this editor wrote itself.
// Caught here, at the one place every caller already funnels through,
// rather than at each of gui_main.d's own many call sites: shows the
// failure directly in the Source pane instead of crashing the whole
// editor over a single unrecognized keyword.
try
  \{
    cvSource.buffer().text(new Writer().generate(roots, ".", i18n, dubHeader, settings));
  \}
catch (Exception e)
  \{
    cvSource.buffer().text("// fluid: could not generate D source:
// " ~ e.msg);
  \}
cvSource.scroll(0, 0);
cvProject.buffer().text(new ProjectWriter().generate(roots, i18n, [], "", null, false, dubHeader, settings));
cvProject.scroll(0, 0);
codeviewUpdatePosition(cvCurrent_);}
      {
      }
  }
Function codeviewAutoRefresh()
  {
    comment {Called after every real project edit -- refreshes the panel if it's
open and Auto-Refresh is on. `gui_main.d` calls this instead of
directly re-checking `codeviewPanel.shown()` at each of its own many
edit call sites, so the Auto-Refresh light button (`cvAutorefresh`)
actually gates something: unchecking it stops these calls from doing
anything, while the "Refresh" button (unconditional) still works.}
    return_type void
    open
  }
  {
    code {if (codeviewPanel is null || !codeviewPanel.shown()) return;
if (cvAutorefresh.value() == 0) return;
codeviewRefresh(cvRoots_, cvI18n_, cvDubHeader_, cvSettings_);}
      {
      }
  }
Function {codeviewToggleVisibility(Node[] roots, I18nSettings i18n = I18nSettings.init, bool dubHeader = false, ProjectSettings settings = ProjectSettings.init)}
  {
    return_type void
  }
  {
    code {if (codeviewPanel is null)
    makeCodeviewPanel();

if (codeviewPanel.shown())
\{
    codeviewPanel.hide();
\}
else
\{
    codeviewPanel.show();
    codeviewRefresh(roots, i18n, dubHeader, settings);
\}}
      {
      }
  }
Function {codeviewUpdatePosition(Node current)}
  {
    return_type void
  }
  {
    code {cvCurrent_ = current;
if (codeviewPanel is null || !codeviewPanel.shown()) return;
if (cvAutoposition.value() == 0) return;
if (current is null) return;

if (cvSource.visibleR())
\{
    int pos0 = -1, pos1 = -1;
    switch (cvCodeChoice.value())
    \{
    case 0: pos0 = current.setupSpan.start; pos1 = current.finalizeSpan.end; break;
    case 1: pos0 = current.setupSpan.start; pos1 = current.setupSpan.end; break;
    case 2: pos0 = current.finalizeSpan.start; pos1 = current.finalizeSpan.end; break;
    default: break;
    \}
    if (pos0 >= 0)
    \{
        auto b = cvSource.buffer();
        if (pos1 < pos0) pos1 = b.lineEnd(pos0);
        b.highlight(pos0, pos1);
        cvSource.scroll(b.countLines(0, pos0), 0);
    \}
\}
if (cvProject.visibleR())
\{
    int pos0 = -1, pos1 = -1;
    switch (cvCodeChoice.value())
    \{
    case 0: pos0 = current.projSpan1.start; pos1 = current.projSpan2.end; break;
    case 1: pos0 = current.projSpan1.start; pos1 = current.projSpan1.end; break;
    case 2: pos0 = current.projSpan2.start; pos1 = current.projSpan2.end; break;
    default: break;
    \}
    if (pos0 >= 0)
    \{
        auto b = cvProject.buffer();
        if (pos1 < pos0) pos1 = b.lineEnd(pos0);
        b.highlight(pos0, pos1);
        cvProject.scroll(b.countLines(0, pos0), 0);
    \}
\}}
      {
      }
  }
Function {findInText(int textType, int pos)}
  {
    return_type Node
  }
  {
    code {Node search(Node[] ns)
\{
    foreach (n; ns)
    \{
        bool hit;
        if (textType == 0)
            hit = (pos >= n.setupSpan.start && pos < n.setupSpan.end)
                || (pos >= n.finalizeSpan.start && pos < n.finalizeSpan.end);
        else
            hit = (pos >= n.projSpan1.start && pos < n.projSpan1.end)
                || (pos >= n.projSpan2.start && pos < n.projSpan2.end);
        if (hit) return n;
        if (auto found = search(n.children)) return found;
    \}
    return null;
\}
return search(cvRoots_);}
      {
      }
  }
